% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 7 "Logic", section 7.9, Example 14 (the Genesis family-tree
%         facts), together with a DECLARATIVE rendering of the ancestor relation
%         of Example 15. The book's Example 15 presents the ancestor relation as
%         forward-chaining production rules; here we encode the same relation as
%         ordinary LE Head-if-Body conditionals (backward-chaining), which is the
%         logically equivalent declarative reading.
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% The concrete Genesis facts (mother-of / father-of) live in the scenario.
% "is a parent of" lifts both mother-of and father-of; "is an ancestor of" is
% the recursive transitive closure. The family tree is a finite DAG, so the
% recursion is well-founded and terminates under tabling. To avoid recursion on
% the same head predicate blocking enumeration (see fox_and_crow.le note 7), the
% primitives mother-of / father-of are kept separate from the derived predicates.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a person* mother of *a second person*.
*a person* father of *a second person*.
*a person* is a parent of *a second person*.
*a person* is an ancestor of *a second person*.

the knowledge base genesis includes:

% A person is a parent of a second person if she is the second person's mother.
a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person mother of the second person.

% A person is a parent of a second person if he is the second person's father.
a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person father of the second person.

% Direct ancestor: a parent is an ancestor.
a person is an ancestor of a second person
    if the person is a parent of the second person.

% Transitive ancestor: a parent of an ancestor is an ancestor.
a person is an ancestor of a second person
    if the person is a parent of a third person
    and the third person is an ancestor of the second person.

scenario genesis is:
    eve mother of cain.
    eve mother of abel.
    adam father of cain.
    adam father of abel.
    cain father of enoch.
    enoch father of irad.
    ancestors expects answers ["enoch is an ancestor of irad", "eve is an ancestor of irad", "adam is an ancestor of irad", "cain is an ancestor of irad"].

query ancestors is:
    which person is an ancestor of irad.
